Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 21:58:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 130/143] config: enable zram (zstd) for low-RAM boards

The 2 GB Orange Pi 4A thrashes to an unresponsive state under a
memory-heavy desktop workload (e.g. a browser playing video): the WebKit
process alone reaches ~700 MB, which drives the board into the on-SD
swapfile whose latency stalls the whole system. Add zram as a module with
a zstd backend so a fast compressed in-RAM swap can be brought up at boot
ahead of the slow SD swapfile. zsmalloc is pulled in automatically.

Modules only; the boot-time zram setup is done in userspace.

Co-Authored-By: AI Agent
---
 arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig
index fe0bcb74e..e71c2202b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig
@@ -209,6 +209,10 @@ CONFIG_MTD_SPI_NOR=y
 CONFIG_MTD_UBI=m
 CONFIG_MTD_HYPERBUS=m
 CONFIG_OF_OVERLAY=y
+CONFIG_ZRAM=m
+CONFIG_ZRAM_BACKEND_ZSTD=y
+CONFIG_ZRAM_BACKEND_LZO=y
+CONFIG_ZRAM_DEF_COMP_ZSTD=y
 CONFIG_BLK_DEV_LOOP=y
 CONFIG_BLK_DEV_NBD=m
 CONFIG_BLK_DEV_NVME=m
